<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armed Forces of South Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Armed Forces of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> were the main White army in southern Russia during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>, formed in January 1919 under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Anton Denikin</a>. Combining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> with the Don and Kuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> forces, they advanced as far as Oryol in October 1919 before being driven back. After Denikin's resignation in 1920, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-wrangel">Pyotr Wrangel</a> reorganised the remnants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armed-forces-of-south-russia.jpg" alt="Armed Forces of South Russia" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Makakaaaa · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%AE%D0%B3_%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%B8.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
